# Sedea user extension project

This repository is a **user bespoke Sedea extension** materialized from [`sedea-extensions/extension-template`](https://github.com/sedea-extensions/extension-template). It is **not** part of the Sedea application monorepo (`sedea-ai/app/extensions/` shipped natives).

## Verify before ship

Run the template verify chain from the repo root:

```bash
npm run verify
```

The script runs lint → typecheck → compile → test. Fix failures before opening a PR.

## Extension Development Host (EDH)

Develop and smoke-test in Sedea's Extension Development Host using this repo as the extension root. Do **not** treat the Sedea app monorepo `extensions/` tree as the destination for feature work in this project.

## MCP contribution manifest

Author `sedea.mcp-contribution.json` using `sedea.mcp-contribution.schema.json` and `sedea.mcp-contribution.example.json` in this repo. **Scaffold does not register runtime MCP** — the **Install Sedea Extension** mission registers contributions on packaged Sedea after VSIX ship.

See [`sedea-mcp-contribution.mdc`](./sedea-mcp-contribution.mdc) for manifest shape and install-time boundaries.

## Post-scaffold feature delivery

After scaffold, use **Software Development `plan and deliver`** in **this user extension repo** for feature work and VSIX ship. Do **not** use **Scaffold New Sedea Extension** as the primary entry for ongoing feature implementation.

## Template maintenance

When platform conventions drift, run sedea center mission **`maintain extension template`** on the hosting stack — not ad-hoc edits to the canonical template without that mission.

Extension slug: `documentation-management-sidecar`
